{
  "imnb_version": 1,
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Raag Khamaj Sitar Composition - Saptak Music School"
  },
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Raag Khamaj",
        "",
        "**Thaat**: Khamaj  ",
        "**Vadi**: Ga  ",
        "**Samvadi**: Ni  ",
        "**Time**: 2nd Prahar of Night (roughly 9:00 PM – 12:00 AM)",
        "",
        "Khamaj is a popular raga known for its romantic and light classical nature (Thumri style). It uses **Shuddha Ni** in Aroha (Ascent) and **Komal Ni** in Avroha (Descent). All other notes are Shuddha.",
        "",
        "This notebook demonstrates all features of the **sargam-v1** language while teaching Raag Khamaj."
      ],
      "id": "68ffc214-7a28-4a6e-aefa-70ed9777d5d3"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 1. Basic Scale: Aroha & Avroha",
        "",
        "**Aroha**: Sa - Ga - Ma - Pa - Dha - Ni - Sa'",
        "",
        "**Avroha**: Sa' - Ni (komal) - Dha - Pa - Ma - Ga - Re - Sa",
        "",
        "",
        "**Aroha**: ",
        "  - Uses Shuddha Ni (N).",
        "  - Banned note: Re",
        "",
        "**Descent**: ",
        "  - Uses Komal Ni (n)."
      ],
      "id": "5242f2f8-6763-4dd4-8241-86fb38843246"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "music",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sargam-v1"
      },
      "source": [
        "@sa D4",
        "@raga Khamaj",
        "",
        "# Aroha (Ascent)",
        "S G M P D N S' ||",
        "",
        "# Avroha (Descent)",
        "S' n D P M G R S ||"
      ],
      "id": "14cab560-c67c-47a5-bfd7-c44d3aec130e"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 2. Composition",
        "",
        "This section presents a Vilambit (slow tempo) composition set to the 16-beat rhythmic cycle known as Teentaal. ",
        "",
        "The melody allows for a detailed exploration of the raga's romantic temperament. "
      ],
      "id": "3f689a5b-9978-4e7c-b710-b3fcda638e1b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "music",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sargam-v1"
      },
      "source": [
        "@sa D4",
        "@tala Tintal(16)",
        "@tala_pattern dha dhin dhin dha | dha dhin dhin dha | dha tin tin ta | ta dhin dhin dha",
        "@tempo 50",
        "",
        "",
        "# Gat / Sthayi / Line 1",
        "",
        ".:4 | .:4 | .3  S:0.5 S:0.5 | G:0.5 ^:0.5 m:0.5 m:0.5 P:0.5 D:0.25 D:0.25 N:0.5 S':0.5 |",
        "N:0.5 ^:0.5 N:0.5 ^:0.5 S':0.5 ^:0.5 n:0.5 n:0.5 | D:0.5 ^:0.5 m:0.5 m:0.5 P:0.5 ^:0.5 D:0.5 ^:0.5 | G:0.5 ^:0.5 m:0.5 ^:0.5 G:0.5 ^:0.5",
        "",
        "# Line 2",
        ".:11 S:0.5 S:0.5 n,:0.5 ^:0.5 S:0.5 S:0.5 m:0.5 ^:0.5 G:0.5 ^:0.5 |",
        "S:0.5 ^:0.5 n,:0.5 ^:0.5 D,:0.5 ^:0.5 P,:0.5 D,:0.5 | N,:0.5 ^:0.5 S:0.5 S:0.5 G:0.5 m:0.25 m:0.25 P:0.5 D:0.5 | G:0.5 ^:0.5 m:0.5 ^:0.5 G:0.5 ^:0.5 |",
        ""
      ],
      "id": "7ce070fa-31a8-441a-b462-498403ae6453"
    },
    {
      "id": "3ee132d7-b4a5-4e4d-844d-cb3cfc8b3c01",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 3. Vilambhit",
        "",
        "This section unfolds in a slow tempo, allowing for expansive melodic development within Teentaal.",
        "",
        "It emphasizes tonal clarity, expressive phrasing, and a deep exploration of the raga’s mood.",
        "",
        "## 3.1 Tan",
        "",
        "This section presents tans in Teentaal, highlighting speed, clarity, and melodic precision.",
        "",
        "The passages maintain the raga’s structure while demonstrating technical control and fluency."
      ]
    },
    {
